s, such as EIRP/EIS spherical coverage. In our view, the UE power consumption would be one significant issue in FR2. Therefore, feasibility of two active UE panels may significantly depend on the UE capability. Test case design is another issue for FR2, especially for RRM. Therefore, it seems quite infeasible to further conclude all the impacts to RRM requirements for this case in R17. There is some discussion on this issue in the pre-meeting discussion for RAN 95e, in [RAN95e-RAN4-R18Prep-02]. It is quite promising that a new RAN4-led WI will be set. Therefore, we think this issue is better to be studied in R18. Proposal 3 In R17 feMIMO WI, simultaneous transmission or reception based on 2 active UE panels is not considered for RRM requirements, and the enhancements of related RRM requirements can be considered in R18 FR2 related RAN4-led WI.

{"chunk_id":"R4-1703895-002","collection":"ran4_tdoc_chunks","metadata":{"source":["Huawei"],"tdocNumber":"R4-1703895","title":"How to update AAS Technical specifications"},"point_id":"4868767116777025028"}
For the eAAS WI the task is to update the existing specification rather than generate a new one so the process will be different to the previous AAS WI. For example as TS 37.105 is an approved document it must be updated with CR’s, and once they are approved then an official version of the updated specification is available. Hence it would be confusing to issue partial updates to the specification to incorporate the OTA requirements. To update the TS documents therefore it would be best to do a single big CR at the end once all the proposed updates have been already drafted and agreed in RAN4. As it is likely to take more than 1 meeting to agree on all the text and procedure where we could write TP’s and pre-approve text for the TS updates would be useful. As such each of the technical specifications which require major modifications for the eAAS WI: TS 37.105 TS 37.145-2 (TS 37.145-2 will at most require minor modifications which can be done by CR directly) TS 37.114 The specifications can then be updated as follows: A draft copy of each specification will be created [2] [3] Modifications to the text regarding the eAAS updates can be submitted like text proposals for RAN4 to approve The rapporteur will update the draft specification after each meeting as a basis for the next. When all the text has been approved by RAN4 the rapporteur will produce a single CR as the final version. The documents can be submitted as discussion documents for approval for example the DRAFT TS: Title: DRAFT TS 37.105 for eAAS updates v1 Type: discussion For: Approval And contributions with text updating the documents could be: Title: TP to DRAFT TS 37.105 on section 9.6.2 Frequency error Type: discussion For: Approval As the work consists of completely new specification text, to avoid having many contributions to each the intention is to use a similar authoring process as was done with REL13 AAS. Sub-authors will be allocated to write the specification text for different sections, that text is reviewed off line as much as practical in between the meetings so that mature text can be presented at the meetings. Sections requiring sub-authors are: For TS 37.104 General sections Huawei (as rapporteur) BS output power (inc control channel power, output power dynamics, Tx ON//OFF power) Transmit signal quality Transmitter UEM Transmitter IMD RX sensitivity Rx interference (inc blocking, ACS, RX IMD) RX unwanted emissions Performance (if possible as in 37.105) For TS 37.114 General sections Huawei (as rapporteur) Emission Immunity The intention is to start updating the text for TS 37.105 and TS37.114 when the technical agreements in the TR are stable, to the following schedule: RAN4#84 Berlin (21-25 Aug) TS 37.105 - BS Output power, TX signal quality, TX UEM, RX sensitivity, RX UEM TS 37.114 - Emissions RAN4#84bis Dubrovnik (9-13Oct) TS 37.105 - General sections, TX IMD, RX interference, Performance TS 37.114 - General sections, Immunity RAN4#85 USA (27Nov-1Dec) Final CR’s As the official versions of the specifications may be modified by CR during the time frame of the process, it is suggested that the DRAFT versions of the specifications stay the same during the process and the final set of modifications are applied to the latest version by the rapporteur in the final CR. This should be straight forward as most of the medications are in the form of new clauses and sub-clauses which will not interfere with any potential CR’s to the existing versions.

